  "roles": "Contract/SDK declare independent compute-worker ownership. R4Pack owns preparation and canonical output. Kernel supplies only thread/producer admission and existing exact lifecycle/VM/FPU mechanics. Spectra extends its existing lifecycle profile.",
  "changes": [
    "runtime.workers=owned-v1 is independent of runtime.parallel. Explicit creation flag1 requires that declaration; unknown bits or missing declaration are unsupported. Main foreground/shell scheduling remains BSP. Zero flags from a main retain legacy behavior; compute descendants inherit their role even with zero flags and on BSP/UP. ThreadInfo exposes separate informational bit8.",
    "ProgramInstance uses former padding byte255, preserving256-byte core and old offsets. Loaded retains1920 bytes/imports offset112. Existing public ABI types/slots/layouts unchanged; exactly two constants and two creation-slot descriptions extend the controlled Contract baseline. Published dependencies are pinned exactly.",
    "Zig and C SDK context/resource facades forward the explicit flag and retain the original owning join handle. R4Pack prepares at most three independent inputs in private job buffers, joins real admitted workers before canonical code/rodata/data assembly and output. Old provider/resource refusal falls back to serial preparation; code-only or --serial stays serial. Original reader/writer bodies are unchanged.",
    "Compute reads do not consume console input; console output is refused/suppressed, host claims and program launches are refused, and GUI production remains with its main owner. Diagnostic probes use original provider tables instead of the userland text adapter. A failed R4Pack join requests terminal exit without returning/releasing the full borrowed main App/Bundle frame or buffers.",
    "Original R4Pack selftest keeps whole self/R4STD inspection with actual-size heap storage bounded16MB independently of unchanged64KB pack/input limit. Exclusive process-generation probe paths, typed delete receipts and confirmed absence govern cleanup. No prior path is overwritten for test setup.",
    "Spectra /WORKERS reuses lifecycle/inventory/wait/reap APIs: one warm Close/Kill pair and one measured pair, two real compute descendants per child, zero-flag inherited role, original console read/write/host/launch refusal and unchanged strict resource/storage baseline. Only successful private /COMPUTEHOLD result records are quiet; failures and ordinary checks retain their output. Field diagnostics preserve the oracle."
  ],
